        host: 'qmyt7hks.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com',
        path: 'api',
      },
      {
        host: 'bkzk-003.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com',
        path: 'ocapi',
      },
      // DW Active Data's __Analytics-Start call (useActiveData.trackPage, base SFCC template
      // code) is built as a relative /mobify/proxy/ocapi/... URL, so it correctly proxies
      // through the 'ocapi' target above — but that target (the Data API host) responds with
      // an HTTP redirect to this instance's separate storefront web host
      // (bkzk-003.my.commercecloud.salesforce.com), a different origin than the 'ocapi'
      // proxy's own configured host. PWA Kit's ssr-proxying.js only rewrites a proxied
      // response's Location header back through the proxy path when the redirect target's
      // origin matches the proxy config's own host (see node_modules/@salesforce/
      // pwa-kit-runtime/utils/ssr-proxying.js's origin check) — since it didn't match here,
      // the raw absolute redirect leaked through and the browser followed it directly,
      // cross-origin, setting the sid/dwsid/dwanonymous_* session cookies there instead of on
      // this app's own domain (confirmed live via a Lighthouse third-party-cookies finding,
      // 2026-09-06/07). Adding this second SFCC host as its own proxy target gives the
      // redirect a matching origin to rewrite against, keeping the whole exchange same-origin.
      // Does NOT address Didomi consent gating for this tracking beacon — Didomi isn't built
      // yet (see .docs/memory/projectState.md); tracked separately.
      //
      // Deliberately SIT-only for now, not yet replicated to config/test.js/uat.js/staging.js/
      // production.js — this fix is itself still unconfirmed working against a real deployed
      // SIT preview (last checked, the same unproxied bkzk-*.my.commercecloud.salesforce.com
      // request was still observed), so copying an unverified fix to four more tiers isn't
      // obviously better than the known gap it would replace. Verify here first, then add the
      // matching `dw` target (same path, that tier's own `bkzk-*` host) to every tier that
      // actually runs DW Active Data — see CodeRabbit review, PR #100, 2026-09-07.
      {
        host: 'bkzk-003.my.commercecloud.salesforce.com',
        path: 'dw',
      },
    ],
  },
};
